{
  "dom_id": "questionContainer",
  "name": "Question 20",
  "problem": "A generator consumes $3$ liters of fuel per hour for the first two hours of use and $5$ liters for each additional hour. Which function $F$ gives the total amount of fuel consumed after $t$ hours, where $t\\ge 2?$",
  "worked_solution": "The total amount of fuel consumed consists of two parts.\n\n- For the first $2$ hours, the generator consumes\n\n$$\n3\\times 2=6\\,\\,\\text{liters}.\n$$\n\n- For each additional hour beyond the first $2,$ the generator consumes\n\n$$\n5(t-2)\\,\\,\\text{liters}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total amount of fuel $F$ consumed after $t$ hours, where $t\\ge 2,$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(t) & =6+5(t-2) \\\\  & =6+5t-10 \\\\  & =5t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
